4. NATURE OF THE OUTPUTS

   The Software is a simulation. Its outputs are conditional projections
   derived from stated assumptions, many of which are unmeasured and are
   swept across ranges rather than fixed. The outputs are not forecasts,
   not predictions, and not statements of expected performance.

